Package: kernel-borderlands
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Kernel Borderlands Team <rushiroyal.k@gmail.com>
Depends: libc6, systemd, openssh-server, libelf1t64 | libelf1, zlib1g
Recommends: python3, python3-venv
Homepage: https://github.com/pardhuvarmax/kernel-borderlands
Description: Kernel-level runtime defense framework (eBPF sensor, control plane, operator tools)
 Kernel Borderlands observes kernel telemetry with eBPF sensors, scores and
 enforces in a Go control plane (kbd), watchdogs the stack with kb-checker,
 and exposes kbctl, an SSH-served TUI and an embedded web dashboard.
 .
 Nothing is started on install. Run `sudo kbctl up`, then `kbctl dashboard
 open` or `kbctl ssh connect`. The kb-aads agent swarm needs a Python venv;
 see /usr/share/doc/kernel-borderlands/README.Debian.
